  ⚠ angular-template(no-outerhtml): Do not use `outerHTML`. Binding to `[outerHTML]` throws on update because setting `outerHTML` replaces the host element itself, so Angular loses its reference to the node ("This element has no parent node"); a static `outerHTML` attribute is not a real DOM attribute and has no effect. Use `[innerHTML]` (being mindful of sanitization) or restructure the
  │ template instead.
   ╭─[no_outerhtml.html:1:7]
 1 │ <div [outerHTML]="html"></div>
   ·       ─────────
